From 1ba3fdeccbc184f8c06e2c676de38aa0cae56dcf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 23:49:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Multi-location fixes: per-location item list, store picker
 UX, header store selector + stroked weather
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Locations tab: per-store availability list now falls back to the full Square
  product list when the app's offered-menu filter is empty, so there is always
  food to tick (fixes '0/0 / Loading products…'). Loading guard mirrors the
  Sold-Out tab.
- Locations tab: one-click 'Add my current store first' seeds the main Square
  location so adding a second store never silently drops it; clearer guidance
  that the customer picker needs two active stores.
- Frontend: header store selector redesigned — stroked storefront icon,
  'Ordering from <store>' with a Change affordance when multiple stores exist,
  static label for a single configured store, and hidden for the synthesised
  single-site default. Weather chip restyled as a matching pill with a stroked
  outline icon and larger text, placed beside the store selector.
- locations.publicList() exposes _default so the client can tell a configured
  single store from the backward-compat synthesised one.
